    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1476">

                <pb facs="1187" n="1071" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1071"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/133.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President of Nicaragua has to-day been authorized by the Assembly to
                    negotiate with American bankers, through the good offices of the United States
                    of America, a loan not exceeding $20,000,000 <pb facs="1188" n="1072"
                        xml:id="pg1072"/> American gold. The Assembly also authorized the President
                    to conclude, subject to ratification by the present Assembly, such treaties and
                    contracts as may be necessary to secure the loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Northcott.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
